"""Approximate the component's lexical contrast between forms of 'person'.

人 and short compounds ending in it are strongly positive. 인 (Korean) and
nhân (Vietnamese) also fire, but some loanwords and 'personal' expressions do
not. English 'person' is negative, with strength depending on the preceding
article, modifier or preposition; 'man'/'men' are mildly positive instead.

