The main positive signal is doubled n, within a small vowel--nn piece or
split across tokens. The main negative signal is n or ns completing compressed
abbreviations such as eqn and soln. Some other consonant+n endings are
negative too. Selected closed Latin syllables and qu
also receive positive values, as does doubled Greek nu. These are spelling
rules, not word meanings.
There are small fixed offsets for doubled middle dots, escaped newlines,
and document starts. Context is the previous token only, reset at document
boundaries; otherwise the prediction is zero.
"""
import re

